.TH XE_TOP 1 "2025-06-05" "xe_top 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xe_top \- Intel Core Ultra full-stack performance monitoring tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xe_top
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xe_top
is a TUI performance monitoring tool for Intel Core Ultra (200V/H/U) processors
on Linux. It provides real-time monitoring of CPU (P-Core/E-Core), Xe Graphics,
NPU, memory bandwidth, power consumption, battery, disk I/O, and network I/O
using Linux PMU (perf_event_open), Uncore IMC, ACPI/RAPL sysfs, and NPU sysfs.
.PP
Most features require root privileges (sudo) to access PMU and RAPL interfaces.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Refresh interval in seconds (default: 1, range: 0.1\-60).
Supports sub-second intervals for high-frequency monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-no-gpu
Disable GPU (Xe Graphics) monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no-cpu
Disable CPU (P-Core/E-Core) monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-no-power
Disable power (RAPL) monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-no-memory
Disable memory (IMC bandwidth + capacity) monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-no-battery
Disable battery monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-no-disk
Disable disk I/O monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-no-net
Disable network I/O monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-no-npu
Disable NPU (AI engine) monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH "INTERACTIVE KEYS"
.TP
.B q " / " Esc
Quit the application.
.TP
.B + " / " \-
Increase/decrease refresh interval by 0.1 seconds.
.TP
.B p
Toggle pause/resume of data collection.
.TP
.B h
Show help information.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 4
Linux kernel 6.18+ with Xe driver PMU support for Intel Core Ultra
(Xe GPU driver was merged into mainline kernel in 6.18)
.IP \(bu 4
Root privileges (sudo) for PMU and RAPL access
.IP \(bu 4
Terminal with UTF-8 support for box-drawing characters
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run with default settings:
sudo xe_top
.TP
Run with 0.5s refresh:
sudo xe_top \-\-interval 0.5
.TP
Disable NPU and battery:
sudo xe_top \-\-no-npu \-\-no-battery
